# LeakSanitizer suppressions for t/run_sanitizers.sh -- the S6 corpus runs
# with leak detection ON since v5.110, and these are the allocations that are
# live at process exit BY CONSTRUCTION, not leaks of any path:
#
#   ngx_js_sw_manager_thread   the SharedWorker manager thread's per-iteration
#                              pollfd array (16 bytes); the thread is parked in
#                              poll() when the worker exits and never returns to
#                              free it.  Joining the thread at exit is its own
#                              change; until then this one frame is named here.
#
# Everything else that LeakSanitizer reports counts.  A suppression is a claim
# ("this is not a leak") and is reviewed like one: add a line here only with the
# reason beside it, and never by function name alone.
leak:ngx_js_sw_manager_thread
